  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change made:**\n```js\nreturn value.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').toLowerCase();\n```\n\n**How it satisfies each requirement:**\n- **Leading/trailing whitespace removed** — `String.prototype.trim()` strips all JavaScript whitespace (spaces, tabs, line breaks) from both ends.\n- **Internal whitespace runs collapsed** — `replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` replaces every nonempty run of whitespace with a single ASCII space. Since trimming happens first, no stray leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- **Lowercased** — `.toLowerCase()` is applied last.\n- **Empty/whitespace-only input** — `trim()` yields `''`, the regex finds no matches, and `''.toLowerCase()` returns `''`.\n- **Non-string input** — the existing `typeof value !== 'string'` guard still throws a `TypeError`.\n\nThe named export `normalizeText` is unchanged, and the public tests (`public.test.mjs`) were not modified. All three test cases pass:\n- `'  HELLO World  '` → `'hello world'`\n- `'One   TWO    Three'` → `'one two three'`\n- `'\\tA\\n \\t B\\r\\nC  '` → `'a b c'`",
